.TH SMARTMON-SNMP-AGENTX 8 "2026-06-13" "smartmontools-@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
smartmon-snmp-agentx \- SNMP AgentX subagent for smartmontools SMART data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smartmon-snmp-agentx
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-\-collect ]
.RB [ \-\-state\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-cache\-timeout
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-state\-db
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR level ]
.RB [ \-\-once ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smartmon-snmp-agentx
is a self-contained Python net-snmp AgentX subagent (RFC 2741) that exposes
SMART drive data via the SMARTMON-* SNMP MIBs.
It requires the
.B python3-netsnmpagent
module.
.PP
It connects to a running
.BR snmpd (8)
master agent over a Unix domain socket, registers the SMARTMON-* OID subtrees,
and responds to SNMP GET/GETNEXT/GETBULK requests.
Trap notifications are sent through the master agent when drive health changes.
.PP
The agent obtains SMART data in one of two ways:
.TP
.B collect mode
With
.B \-\-collect
(or
.B collect=true
in the config) the agent polls
.BR smartctl (8)
directly.
It runs smartctl as root when the agent is root, otherwise via
.BR "sudo \-n smartctl" .
No
.B state_dir
is required.
.TP
.B file mode (default)
The agent reads JSON state files from
.B state_dir
written by the
.B smartmon-collect
timer or by
.BR smartd (8)
configured with
.BR \-\-jsonstate .
It will not start unless
.B state_dir
is set.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " config" "\fR, \fP" \-\-config " config"
Path to configuration file.
Default:
.IR @sysconfdir@/smartmontools/snmp-agentx.yaml .
.TP
.B \-f
Run in the foreground; do not daemonise.
.TP
.B \-\-collect
Poll
.BR smartctl (8)
directly instead of reading
.BR state_dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " dir"
Directory containing smartd
.B \-\-jsonstate
JSON files (file mode).
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-timeout " seconds"
Data refresh / poll interval.
In file mode, how long parsed data is cached before re-reading; in collect
mode, the smartctl poll interval.
Config key:
.BR cache_timeout .
Default: 300.
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-db " path"
SQLite file persisting table change timestamps and notification baselines
across restarts.
Unset disables persistence.
.TP
.BI \-\-agentx\-socket " path"
AgentX master socket path.
Must match
.B agentXSocket
in
.IR snmpd.conf (5).
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
Minimum log severity:
.BR DEBUG ", " VERBOSE ", " INFO ", " NOTICE ", " WARNING ", " ERROR .
Default:
.BR WARNING .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " path"
Append log output to this file in addition to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Collect and publish once, then exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.I @sysconfdir@/smartmontools/snmp-agentx.yaml
(or the file given with
.BR \-c ),
which is YAML.
A plain
.RB \(dq "key value" \(dq
key/value file is also accepted.
.TP
.BI collect " bool"
Poll smartctl directly when
.BR true .
Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.BI state_dir " path"
Directory of smartd JSON state files
.RB ( Required
in file mode).
.TP
.BI agentx_socket " path"
AgentX master socket.
Default:
.IR /var/agentx/master .
.TP
.BI cache_timeout " seconds"
Data refresh / poll interval.
Default: 300.
.TP
.BI state_db " path"
SQLite persistence file.
Unset disables persistence.
.TP
.BI poll_failure_threshold " n"
Consecutive poll failures before a
.B smartmonDevicePollFailed
trap fires.
Default: 1.
.TP
.BI sensor_hysteresis " units"
Hysteresis applied when clearing a sensor alarm.
Default: 0.
.TP
.BI sensor_resend_interval " seconds"
Re-send a persistent sensor alarm trap every N seconds.
0 disables.
Default: 0.
.SH SMARTD CONFIGURATION
When using
.BR smartd (8)
to produce the JSON files (file mode), it must be configured with the
.B \-x
(extended) flag so that all data required by the MIBs is present, including
NVMe self-test logs and SAS error counter logs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
DEVICESCAN -x --jsonstate /run/smartmontools/json/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Using
.B \-a
instead of
.B \-x
omits NVMe self-test log entries and SAS error counters; those MIB tables
will be empty.
The
.B smartmon-collect
timer is an alternative that calls smartctl directly and needs no smartd
configuration.
.SH SNMPD CONFIGURATION
Add the following to
.IR /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf :
.PP
.RS
.nf
master agentx
agentXSocket /var/agentx/master
agentXPerms 0660 0550 root Debian-snmp
rocommunity public 127.0.0.1 .1.3.6.1.4.1.9999
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @sysconfdir@/smartmontools/snmp-agentx.yaml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /run/smartmontools/json/
Recommended location for JSON state files (file mode).
.TP
.I /var/agentx/master
Default AgentX master socket.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Initiates shutdown: stops the collector thread, closes the state database,
and exits.
.SH EXIT STATUS
A non-zero exit indicates a startup problem: a configuration error (for
example
.B state_dir
unset in file mode), a missing
.B python3-netsnmpagent
dependency, or an AgentX connection failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartd (8),
.BR smartd.conf (5),
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR snmpd (8),
.BR snmpd.conf (5)
.SH AUTHORS
smartmontools development team.
See
.I https://www.smartmontools.org/
for details.
